{
  "case_id": "2008-07-463",
  "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit's affirmance of a nationwide injunction in this case is contrary to bedrock principles of Article III standing, of the availability and scope of judicial review under the Administrative Procedure Act, and the granting of equitable relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Standing itself, I mean, it's a little unusual. Suppose -- I mean, Congress here has passed a statute and the statute specifically aims at a class of litigants. And it says to the class of litigants, if you are a member of it, we are telling you what we want the agency to do and that is to promulgate a certain appeal procedure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Mr. Kneedler, don't we have to assess the need for -- for showing a specific threatened injury on a -- on a somewhat elastic standard in a case like this? Because the claim is made on the other side that if we do not allow, if we do not find standing to challenge the regulation per se, there are going to be a number of specific instances which in practical terms can never be challenged when that regulation is applied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is the so-called Schedule Of Proposed Actions, which includes all the actions in which there would be a decision memo issued by the Forest Service, which includes at least all of the projects that respondents are claiming should be -- should be covered. That is published quarterly. It -- it is available on the web. It is also available in person."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could any one of those have brought suit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The procedural regulation does not cause the injury. It is the on-the-ground activity, the site-specific decision -- the action, the agency action approving the site-specific action that causes the injury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0001-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "An injunction, a preliminary injunction was obtained, and tellingly, and I think this is also instructive for ripeness purposes, there was a PI issued but not because of a violation of the -- of the ARA; the district court concluded there was a likelihood of success on some of these other objections, substantive objections to the project, not procedural objections --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And here the agency's procedures allow somebody to request to be put on the mailing list about a particular project."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's the -- that's the only kind of additional notice the statute ever provides for."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Will you have standing to challenge that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would be your standard for when you need notice and comment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is, it says, \"a proposed decision implementing a forest plan shall be made subject to notice and comment.\" And then section C states that \"any decision approving such an action shall be subject to appeal.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You need a permit to have a Christmas tree? Where is this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Kenna)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, that is exempt, not because it's environmentally insignificant, which, you know, it probably is in most cases, but because there is no decision approving it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Kenna)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5994ac6a32193f87c7d1c01a5202092a9405118bc0915a9a6d715020ea3121f1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5994ac6a3219-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Blum v. Yaretsky, and that we cite in our brief; and then Northeastern Florida Chamber of Contractors v. Jacksonville. That's a 1993 case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-463",
      "confidence": 0.0,
